# STIG CD16-00-011300: PostgreSQL must generate audit records when unsuccessful logons or connection at
# STIG ID: V-261957 (MEDIUM)

META
    esp_id `pg16-cd16-00-011300-audit-failed-logons-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `pg16`
    criticality `high`

    title `STIG CD16-00-011300: PostgreSQL must generate audit records when unsuccessful logons or connection at`
    description `PostgreSQL must generate audit records when unsuccessful logons or connection attempts occur.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `pg16,stig,disa-stig`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:CD16-00-011300,NIST-800-53:AU-12`
    control_objective `AU-12`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `dba`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `PostgreSQL16:localhost:pg-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Review and configure the required PostgreSQL parameters to meet compliance requirements.`

    component_id `comp-pg16-db`

    impl_AU_12 `PostgreSQL implements this control by validating the required configuration parameters are set to compliant values. The pg_config_param contract queries each parameter via SHOW and compares against the expected state.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT pg_param
        parameter `log_connections`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE param_state
        value string = `on`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN pg_config_param
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF param_state
            OBJECT_REF pg_param
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
